<Main
	image="/images/profile.png"
	imageAlt="Michael DeVito"
>
	<h1>Hello World!</h1>
	<p>
		My name is Michael, and welcome to my personal portfolio. I am a Senior Cybersecurity Major at Messiah University, with a minor in Web Development.
		I plan to graduate in the Spring 2027 semester, and I am currently seeking an entry-level position within the cybersecurity field.
		Here is a collection of writeups and blog-style posts about my cybersecurity journey. All directories can be accessed via the terminal on the left!
	</p>
	<br>
	<br>
	<h2>About Me</h2>
	<p>
		Ever since middle school, when I was the unofficial "technological consultant" fixing laptops and tablets, I have been invested in all aspects of information technology.
		However, it was in high school that I realized my love for cybersecurity, specifically cyber defense. As I've grown in knowledge and experience through my time at Messiah University, I've found that my
		passion lies in system administration and network security, which is evident through my personal projecs, coursework, and internship experience.
	</p>
	<p>
		While at Messiah, I am an intern in the Security Operations Center, an on-campus internship offered to Cybersecurity students that provides SIEM-based log analysis experience
		using real-world network traffic from the campus. I am currently in my third consecutive semester of this internship, in which I have pivoted to Development Team Leader,
		where I get to utilize skills gained with my Web Development minor to help improve and troubleshoot internal websites in use at Messiah. Outside of work, I am
		a co-captain for the Messiah Cyber Competition Club, a space where students can train for cybersecurity competitions. Our most notable competition is the Collegate Cyber Defense Competition (CCDC), in 
		which we compete yearly. We also compete in the NCL and NCAE competitions in the Fall and Spring, respectively.
	</p>
	<p>
		In my free time, I enjoy working on my homelab, reading, and playing videogames. I am also developing a hobby for collecting physical media, including Blu-Rays, DVDs, and CDs. 
	</p>

</Main>